{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversion resolution versus accuracy conversion resolution versus accuracy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","fileName":"Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Significant Digits in Unit Conversion","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conversion resolution versus accuracy conversion resolution versus accuracy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","fileName":"Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy","heading":"Conversion Resolution versus Accuracy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Resolution is the number of digits presented in a measurement or calculation; accuracy concerns how well those digits represent the intended quantity. The book warns that a conversion result with many displayed places can appear more trustworthy than the starting observation warrants. It gives 1000 as an ambiguous example: the app initially reads four significant digits, but an estimate to the nearest thousand should be reported with only one. The user must supply that context because the digi